# Vulnerability details

### Impact
An attacker can exploit the `initProject` function by front-running the actual `project admin`, preventing them from successfully launching the project and associated `ILO pools`. 

The attacker can DoS or render the project into an unusable state (as the attacker will not be able to initiate associated `ILO pools` and the launch project) as a result the legitimate `project admin` will be unable to launch the project or `ILO pools`, therefore effectively causing a denial of service (DoS).

### Proof of Concept
* The actual `project admin` or `Owner` calls `initProject()`
* Attacker sees and front-runs the `project owner`
* Attacker successfully becomes `project admin` via `initProject()`
* The actual `project owner` tries to call `initProject()` again but reverts because of this check `require(_project.uniV3PoolAddress != address(0), "NI")` (i.e cannot call `initProject()` more than once)
* Although since the attacker does not have the `SALE_TOKEN` to launch, they only successfully DoS the actual `project admin` or `Owner` from launching the project and associated `ILO pools`. 

