## Impact
In ILOPool.sol contract, with launch() function, the manager can launchs pools before launchTime and saleTime, allowing users to buy even after the launch. This is not intended by the protocol.


## Proof of Concept
Add this functions in your ILOPool.t.sol file : 

    function _launchBeforeSaleEnd() internal {
        _prepareBuyFor(INVESTOR);
        _buyFor(INVESTOR, SALE_START+1, 49000 ether);
        _prepareBuyFor(INVESTOR_2);
        _buyFor(INVESTOR_2, SALE_START+1, 40000 ether);
        _buyFor(INVESTOR, SALE_START+1, 1000 ether);
        _writeTokenBalance(SALE_TOKEN, iloPool, 95000 * 4 ether);

       //We can use the launch just after SALE_START and before SALE_END.
        vm.warp(SALE_START + 1);
        vm.prank(address(iloManager));
        IILOPool(iloPool).launch();
    }

    function testBuyAfterLaunch() external {
        _launchBeforeSaleEnd();

        _prepareBuy();
        uint256 balanceBefore = IERC20(USDC).balanceOf(iloPool);

        (uint256 tokenId, uint128 liquidity) = _buy(SALE_START+1, 0.1 ether);

        uint256 balanceAfter = IERC20(USDC).balanceOf(iloPool);

        assertEq(balanceAfter - balanceBefore, 0.1 ether);
    }

In _launchBeforeSaleEnd() the manager can launch before launchTime and saleTime. Then in testBuyAfterLaunch(), after calling _launchBeforeSaleEnd(), the contract can buy again.


