The following `ILOManager.launch` function iterates over all of the corresponding project's initialized ilo pools and calls each pool's `ILOPool.launch` function below. Since the `ILOPool.launch` function further calls multiple other functions, such as `_saleAmountNeeded`, `addLiquidity`, `_mint`, and `_refundProject`, and iterates over `_vestingConfigs` and `schedule` of each `_vestingConfigs[index]`, the gas usage for the `ILOPool.launch` function call can be considerable. Because there is no upper limit on the number of ilo pools that can be initialized for a project, considerable number of ilo pools can be initialized for the corresponding project; calling the `ILOManager.launch` function, which needs to launch each of these ilo pools, can run out of gas even though all of these ilo pools' `softCap` are reached after enough purchases are made for these pools. Thus, the project and all of its pools can be DOS'ed from being launched due to gas running out.

